 law and political theory, and simply take for granted the existence of an Islamic state in whatever form they themselves knew it." Abu Hamid Muhammad al-Ghazali (1058-1111 CE): "Theologian and philosopher from Tus in what is now Iranian Khurasan, and author of The Incoherence of the Philosophers, which threw down the gauntlet to rationalism."  Ḥasan Ghaznavi wrote philosophy in Arabic and Persian.  Nizam al-Mulk (1018-1092 CE) (or Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali) a "powerful Seljuk vizier from Tus who railed against the Ismailis in his Book of Government"  Ghazali (1058-1111 CE). '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1850, 'temperature': 0.2})
